              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "You can log in to your **My Service Canada Account (MSCA)** securely through the official Government of Canada portal. \n\n### 1. Official Login Link\nAccess the official login page directly:\n* \ud83d\udc49 **[canada.ca/MyServiceCanadaAccount](https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/services/my-account.html)**\n\n---\n\n### 2. Choose Your Sign-In Method\nOnce you are on the landing page, click the **\"Sign in to MSCA\"** button. You will be prompted to choose one of three secure methods to log in:\n\n* **Option 1: GCKey** \n  * Select this if you have a government-issued GCKey username and password. (If you don't have one, you can register for a GCKey on the same page).\n* **Option 2: Sign-In Partner (Interac Sign-In Service)** \n  * This allows you to log in securely using your Canadian online banking credentials (e.g., RBC, TD, Scotiabank, BMO, CIBC, etc.). *Note: The government will not see your banking transactions, and your bank will not see your government information\u2014it is used strictly to verify your identity.*\n* **Option 3: Provincial Digital ID** \n  * If you reside in **Alberta** or **British Columbia**, you can sign in using your **Alberta.ca Account** or **BC Services Card**.\n\n---\n\n### 3. What You Can Access Once Logged In\nOnce inside your dashboard, you can view and manage:\n* **Employment Insurance (EI):** Check application status, view payments, view electronic Records of Employment (ROEs), and access T4E tax slips.\n* **Canada Pension Plan (CPP) & Old Age Security (OAS):** Estimate retirement pensions, track application status, view monthly payments, and get T4A tax slips.\n* **Canadian Dental Care Plan (CDCP):** Manage and view your coverage information.\n* **Profile & Banking:** Update your home address, phone number, and direct deposit banking information across multiple services.\n\n---\n\n### \u26a0\ufe0f Security Reminders\n* **Check the Web Address:** Always verify that the website URL begins with **`https://...canada.ca`** to ensure you are on a legitimate government site and not a phishing replica.\n* **Avoid Scams:** Service Canada will **never** send you an email or text message asking you to click a link to input your Social Insurance Number (SIN), passwords, or bank details. If you receive such a message, delete it immediately.",
